The forward lens copies an optional, unbounded field (from.count, line 7 of
1.0) into a required, bounded one (count: int & <10, line 3), and the data
(count: 20) violates the bound. Before lens totality was proven at bind, only
Translate found it, and positioned the error at the bound and the data, never
at the mapping that carried the value; a second error from the comprehension
in translate.cue added a kernel position.

Bind now refuses the lens (checkLensTotality), with two findings at the
mapping: the copy is narrowed (the source accepts 20, the target does not),
and its source may be absent. Every position is authored. The translate-time
shape is no longer reachable from a bound lineage.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
schema: {
	title: string
	count?: int
}
-- ship/history/1.0.thema --
schema: {
	title: string
	count: int & <10
}

forward: {
	count: from.count
}

backward: {
	count: to.count
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
schema: {
	title: string
	count: int & <10
}

forward: {
	count: from.count
}

backward: {
	count: to.count
}
-- data.json --
{"title": "a", "count": 20}
-- out/error --
count in the result of lens v0.0->v1.0 copies v0_0.count, which is now int & <10, which does not accept every value of the prior int:
    ship/history/1.0.thema:7:9
count in the result of lens v0.0->v1.0 copies v0_0.count, which may be absent: v0_0.count is optional in the source schema:
    ship/history/1.0.thema:7:9
-- out/positions --
count in the result of lens v0.0->v1.0 copies v0_0.count, which is now int & <10, which does not accept every value of the prior int
	authored ship/history/1.0.thema:7:9
count in the result of lens v0.0->v1.0 copies v0_0.count, which may be absent: v0_0.count is optional in the source schema
